{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Submitted a synthesizable AXI4-Lite timer RTL (axil_timer.v) and a self-checking testbench (axil_timer_tb.v) that runs ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8 instances in lockstep. No formal_spec file is included. Lint, simulation and synthesis are left to the platform's own runs.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "design_note", "title": "Implementation decisions and spec trace for axil_timer", "summary": "Channels follow [artifact:prj-79e7446228.microarchitecture.a1] section 1: awready = !aw_held && !bvalid, wready = !w_held && !bvalid, arready = !rvalid, and do_write when both write halves are present. The timer next state is one combinational block applied in the order given in section 2 (count step, then expired clear, then expired set, then CTRL write, then LOAD byte merge). This gives the priorities of [artifact:prj-79e7446228.interface-spec.a1] section 4: a count end beats a clear, and a CTRL write wins for EN and COUNT. The decode is addr[1:0]==0 and zero above bit 3 (section 3), done on a 32-bit zero-extended address so it is the same at every ADDR_WIDTH from 4 to 8. Reset is synchronous and active low. One recorded deviation: the held address, data and strobe flops are also reset. The microarchitecture says they need no reset; resetting them is a strict superset, chosen to keep every flop reset and avoid reset gaps. Traces to [requirement:req-2b2b91a584]."}], "files": [{"path": "axil_timer.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "axil_timer RTL", "summary": "AXI4-Lite subordinate timer implementing [artifact:prj-79e7446228.interface-spec.a1] as planned in [artifact:prj-79e7446228.microarchitecture.a1]. It has independent AW/W holding, single-outstanding B and R, SLVERR for COUNT writes and unmapped or unaligned addresses, and zero read data for unmapped reads. Registers are CTRL (EN, IE, MODE), LOAD with byte strobes, read-only COUNT, and STATUS (write 1 to clear EXPIRED). One-shot and periodic modes are supported, with count_end = en && count<=1. irq = expired && ie. Only synchronous active-low reset is used; there are no latches by construction (every combinational output has a default). A few invariants sit under ifdef FORMAL. Serves [requirement:req-2b2b91a584].", "entry": "axil_timer"}, {"path": "axil_timer_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "axil_timer self-checking testbench", "summary": "Directed self-checking testbench covering the section 8 list in [artifact:prj-79e7446228.interface-spec.a1]:\n- reset values, and LOAD partial strobes including an empty strobe;\n- AW-first, W-first, together and back-to-back writes, B and R backpressure, and a read and a write on the same clock;\n- the COUNT read-only SLVERR, unaligned SLVERR, and offsets 0x10 to 0xFC at ADDR_WIDTH 8;\n- a CTRL write without wstrb[0], and STATUS writes of 0 or without strobe;\n- one-shot counts at LOAD 5, 1 and 0 timed to the edge, with EN self-clear and no second interrupt;\n- IE written on a pending expiry;\n- periodic timing over several periods, with a clear landing on a count-end edge;\n- stop freezing COUNT, a restart, CTRL start and stop on a count-end edge, and reset during a count clearing a held AW.\n\nTiming is measured from the write's effect edge, following [artifact:prj-79e7446228.microarchitecture.a1] section 5. An ADDR_WIDTH 4 instance runs in lockstep and is compared output by output. Failures use $error. It ends with the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line read from the nirmaan_nonce plusarg.", "entry": "axil_timer_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The RTL is expected to be clean under Verilator --lint-only -Wall; this has not been run.", "The testbench is expected to pass against this RTL under Icarus Verilog (SystemVerilog mode for $error) and Verilator (needs --timing with --binary or --main); this has not been run.", "The design is expected to synthesize in Yosys without latches; this has not been run.", "The expected timing (a count started on edge E with LOAD N ends on edge E+N, and periodic counts end at E+kN) was derived by hand from the interface spec. It is not verified."], "escalation": null, "notes": "1. No formal_spec is submitted, so formal.run and formal.cover do not apply to this task. However, interface_spec section 8 and microarchitecture section 5 call for an unbounded proof at ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8. That requirement is still open and should be tracked as a follow-up task. The ifdef FORMAL invariants in the RTL are design intent only and have not been proven.\n2. The testbench drives inputs and samples outputs on the falling edge. It counts rising edges in a clocked monitor. The ADDR_WIDTH 4 lockstep comparison is switched off only during the 0x10-and-above unmapped test, because those addresses alias at width 4; both instances are reset afterwards.\n3. The held address, data and strobe flops are reset. This is a deviation from the microarchitecture, which says they need no reset. It is recorded here and does not change behaviour.\n4. If the platform's simulator is Verilator, the testbench needs timing support (--timing, with --binary or --main) for the plusarg and the delays."}

=== FILE: axil_timer.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
// axil_timer: 32-bit down-counting timer with one-shot and periodic modes
// and a level interrupt, behind an AXI4-Lite subordinate port.
// Implements interface_spec.md as planned in microarchitecture.md.
module axil_timer #(
    parameter integer ADDR_WIDTH = 4
) (
    input  wire                  aclk,
    input  wire                  aresetn,
    input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] s_axil_awaddr,
    input  wire                  s_axil_awvalid,
    output wire                  s_axil_awready,
    input  wire [31:0]           s_axil_wdata,
    input  wire [3:0]            s_axil_wstrb,
    input  wire                  s_axil_wvalid,
    output wire                  s_axil_wready,
    output wire [1:0]            s_axil_bresp,
    output wire                  s_axil_bvalid,
    input  wire                  s_axil_bready,
    input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] s_axil_araddr,
    input  wire                  s_axil_arvalid,
    output wire                  s_axil_arready,
    output wire [31:0]           s_axil_rdata,
    output wire [1:0]            s_axil_rresp,
    output wire                  s_axil_rvalid,
    input  wire                  s_axil_rready,
    output wire                  irq
);

  localparam [1:0] RESP_OKAY   = 2'b00;
  localparam [1:0] RESP_SLVERR = 2'b10;

  localparam [1:0] IDX_CTRL   = 2'd0;
  localparam [1:0] IDX_LOAD   = 2'd1;
  localparam [1:0] IDX_COUNT  = 2'd2;
  localparam [1:0] IDX_STATUS = 2'd3;

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Channel state
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  reg                  aw_held_q;
  reg                  w_held_q;
  reg [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] aw_addr_q;
  reg [31:0]           w_data_q;
  reg [3:0]            w_strb_q;
  reg                  bvalid_q;
  reg [1:0]            bresp_q;
  reg                  rvalid_q;
  reg [31:0]           rdata_q;
  reg [1:0]            rresp_q;

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Timer state and its next-state values
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  reg        en_q;
  reg        ie_q;
  reg        mode_q;
  reg        expired_q;
  reg [31:0] load_q;
  reg [31:0] count_q;

  reg        en_d;
  reg        ie_d;
  reg        mode_d;
  reg        expired_d;
  reg [31:0] load_d;
  reg [31:0] count_d;

  reg [31:0] rd_value;

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Handshakes (READY depends on flops only)
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  wire awready  = !aw_held_q && !bvalid_q;
  wire wready   = !w_held_q && !bvalid_q;
  wire arready  = !rvalid_q;

  wire aw_hs    = s_axil_awvalid && awready;
  wire w_hs     = s_axil_wvalid && wready;
  wire ar_hs    = s_axil_arvalid && arready;

  wire do_write = (aw_held_q || aw_hs) && (w_held_q || w_hs);

  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] wr_addr = aw_held_q ? aw_addr_q : s_axil_awaddr;
  wire [31:0]           wr_data = w_held_q ? w_data_q : s_axil_wdata;
  wire [3:0]            wr_strb = w_held_q ? w_strb_q : s_axil_wstrb;

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Address decode: mapped only when word aligned and below 0x10
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  wire [31:0] wr_addr_ext = {{(32-ADDR_WIDTH){1'b0}}, wr_addr};
  wire [31:0] rd_addr_ext = {{(32-ADDR_WIDTH){1'b0}}, s_axil_araddr};

  wire wr_mapped = (wr_addr_ext[1:0] == 2'b00) && (wr_addr_ext[31:4] == 28'd0);
  wire rd_mapped = (rd_addr_ext[1:0] == 2'b00) && (rd_addr_ext[31:4] == 28'd0);

  wire [1:0] wr_idx = wr_addr_ext[3:2];
  wire [1:0] rd_idx = rd_addr_ext[3:2];

  wire [1:0] wr_resp = (wr_mapped && (wr_idx != IDX_COUNT)) ? RESP_OKAY : RESP_SLVERR;
  wire [1:0] rd_resp = rd_mapped ? RESP_OKAY : RESP_SLVERR;

  wire ctrl_wr    = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == IDX_CTRL) && wr_strb[0];
  wire load_wr    = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == IDX_LOAD);
  wire status_clr = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == IDX_STATUS) &&
                    wr_strb[0] && wr_data[0];

  // End of count: EN set and COUNT at 1 or 0
  wire count_end = en_q && (count_q[31:1] == 31'd0);

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Read data mux
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  always @* begin
    rd_value = 32'd0;
    case (rd_idx)
      IDX_CTRL:   rd_value = {29'd0, mode_q, ie_q, en_q};
      IDX_LOAD:   rd_value = load_q;
      IDX_COUNT:  rd_value = count_q;
      IDX_STATUS: rd_value = {31'd0, expired_q};
      default:    rd_value = 32'd0;
    endcase
    if (!rd_mapped) begin
      rd_value = 32'd0;
    end
  end

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Timer next state: order gives the spec priorities
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  always @* begin
    en_d      = en_q;
    ie_d      = ie_q;
    mode_d    = mode_q;
    expired_d = expired_q;
    load_d    = load_q;
    count_d   = count_q;

    // 1. Count step
    if (en_q) begin
      if (count_end) begin
        if (mode_q) begin
          count_d = load_q;
        end else begin
          count_d = 32'd0;
          en_d    = 1'b0;
        end
      end else begin
        count_d = count_q - 32'd1;
      end
    end

    // 2. EXPIRED: clear first, then a count end sets it (end beats clear)
    if (status_clr) begin
      expired_d = 1'b0;
    end
    if (count_end) begin
      expired_d = 1'b1;
    end

    // 3. CTRL write wins for EN and COUNT
    if (ctrl_wr) begin
      ie_d   = wr_data[1];
      mode_d = wr_data[2];
      if (wr_data[0]) begin
        en_d    = 1'b1;
        count_d = load_q;
      end else begin
        en_d = 1'b0;
      end
    end

    // 4. LOAD byte merge
    if (load_wr) begin
      if (wr_strb[0]) load_d[7:0]   = wr_data[7:0];
      if (wr_strb[1]) load_d[15:8]  = wr_data[15:8];
      if (wr_strb[2]) load_d[23:16] = wr_data[23:16];
      if (wr_strb[3]) load_d[31:24] = wr_data[31:24];
    end
  end

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Timer registers
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  always @(posedge aclk) begin
    if (!aresetn) begin
      en_q      <= 1'b0;
      ie_q      <= 1'b0;
      mode_q    <= 1'b0;
      expired_q <= 1'b0;
      load_q    <= 32'd0;
      count_q   <= 32'd0;
    end else begin
      en_q      <= en_d;
      ie_q      <= ie_d;
      mode_q    <= mode_d;
      expired_q <= expired_d;
      load_q    <= load_d;
      count_q   <= count_d;
    end
  end

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Write channels
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  always @(posedge aclk) begin
    if (!aresetn) begin
      aw_held_q <= 1'b0;
      w_held_q  <= 1'b0;
      aw_addr_q <= {ADDR_WIDTH{1'b0}};
      w_data_q  <= 32'd0;
      w_strb_q  <= 4'd0;
      bvalid_q  <= 1'b0;
      bresp_q   <= RESP_OKAY;
    end else begin
      if (do_write) begin
        aw_held_q <= 1'b0;
        w_held_q  <= 1'b0;
        bvalid_q  <= 1'b1;
        bresp_q   <= wr_resp;
      end else begin
        if (aw_hs) begin
          aw_held_q <= 1'b1;
          aw_addr_q <= s_axil_awaddr;
        end
        if (w_hs) begin
          w_held_q <= 1'b1;
          w_data_q <= s_axil_wdata;
          w_strb_q <= s_axil_wstrb;
        end
        if (bvalid_q && s_axil_bready) begin
          bvalid_q <= 1'b0;
        end
      end
    end
  end

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Read channels
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  always @(posedge aclk) begin
    if (!aresetn) begin
      rvalid_q <= 1'b0;
      rdata_q  <= 32'd0;
      rresp_q  <= RESP_OKAY;
    end else if (ar_hs) begin
      rvalid_q <= 1'b1;
      rdata_q  <= rd_value;
      rresp_q  <= rd_resp;
    end else if (rvalid_q && s_axil_rready) begin
      rvalid_q <= 1'b0;
    end
  end

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Outputs
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  assign s_axil_awready = awready;
  assign s_axil_wready  = wready;
  assign s_axil_bvalid  = bvalid_q;
  assign s_axil_bresp   = bresp_q;
  assign s_axil_arready = arready;
  assign s_axil_rvalid  = rvalid_q;
  assign s_axil_rdata   = rdata_q;
  assign s_axil_rresp   = rresp_q;
  assign irq            = expired_q && ie_q;

`ifdef FORMAL
  // Design-intent invariants, valid once reset has been applied.
  reg f_reset_seen;
  initial f_reset_seen = 1'b0;
  always @(posedge aclk) begin
    if (!aresetn) begin
      f_reset_seen <= 1'b1;
    end
  end
  always @(*) begin
    if (f_reset_seen) begin
      assert(!(aw_held_q && w_held_q));
      if (bvalid_q) assert(!aw_held_q && !w_held_q);
      assert((bresp_q == RESP_OKAY) || (bresp_q == RESP_SLVERR));
      assert((rresp_q == RESP_OKAY) || (rresp_q == RESP_SLVERR));
    end
  end
`endif

endmodule
=== END FILE ===
=== FILE: axil_timer_tb.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
// Self-checking testbench for axil_timer. Runs an ADDR_WIDTH 8 instance
// (checked against expectations) and an ADDR_WIDTH 4 instance in lockstep.
module axil_timer_tb;

  localparam [1:0] OKAY   = 2'b00;
  localparam [1:0] SLVERR = 2'b10;

  reg        clk     = 1'b0;
  reg        aresetn = 1'b0;
  reg [7:0]  awaddr  = 8'd0;
  reg        awvalid = 1'b0;
  reg [31:0] wdata   = 32'd0;
  reg [3:0]  wstrb   = 4'd0;
  reg        wvalid  = 1'b0;
  reg        bready  = 1'b0;
  reg [7:0]  araddr  = 8'd0;
  reg        arvalid = 1'b0;
  reg        rready  = 1'b0;

  wire        awready8, wready8, bvalid8, arready8, rvalid8, irq8;
  wire [1:0]  bresp8, rresp8;
  wire [31:0] rdata8;
  wire        awready4, wready4, bvalid4, arready4, rvalid4, irq4;
  wire [1:0]  bresp4, rresp4;
  wire [31:0] rdata4;

  axil_timer #(.ADDR_WIDTH(8)) dut8 (
      .aclk(clk), .aresetn(aresetn),
      .s_axil_awaddr(awaddr), .s_axil_awvalid(awvalid), .s_axil_awready(awready8),
      .s_axil_wdata(wdata), .s_axil_wstrb(wstrb), .s_axil_wvalid(wvalid), .s_axil_wready(wready8),
      .s_axil_bresp(bresp8), .s_axil_bvalid(bvalid8), .s_axil_bready(bready),
      .s_axil_araddr(araddr), .s_axil_arvalid(arvalid), .s_axil_arready(arready8),
      .s_axil_rdata(rdata8), .s_axil_rresp(rresp8), .s_axil_rvalid(rvalid8), .s_axil_rready(rready),
      .irq(irq8)
  );

  axil_timer #(.ADDR_WIDTH(4)) dut4 (
      .aclk(clk), .aresetn(aresetn),
      .s_axil_awaddr(awaddr[3:0]), .s_axil_awvalid(awvalid), .s_axil_awready(awready4),
      .s_axil_wdata(wdata), .s_axil_wstrb(wstrb), .s_axil_wvalid(wvalid), .s_axil_wready(wready4),
      .s_axil_bresp(bresp4), .s_axil_bvalid(bvalid4), .s_axil_bready(bready),
      .s_axil_araddr(araddr[3:0]), .s_axil_arvalid(arvalid), .s_axil_arready(arready4),
      .s_axil_rdata(rdata4), .s_axil_rresp(rresp4), .s_axil_rvalid(rvalid4), .s_axil_rready(rready),
      .irq(irq4)
  );

  integer passed        = 0;
  integer failed        = 0;
  integer lock_pass     = 0;
  integer lock_fail     = 0;
  integer edge_cnt      = 0;
  integer irq_rises     = 0;
  integer irq_rise_edge = -1;
  reg     irq_last      = 1'b0;
  reg     lock_en       = 1'b0;
  integer wr_eff        = 0;
  integer rd_edge       = 0;
  reg [31:0] rd_data    = 32'd0;
  reg [1:0]  rd_resp    = 2'd0;
  reg [8*64-1:0] nonce  = {(8*64){1'b0}};
  integer plus_ok       = 0;
  integer e0, e1, e2, s0, prev, p, exp_cnt;

  always #5 clk = ~clk;

  // Edge counter and interrupt-rise monitor. At posedge k the values read
  // are those after edge k-1, and edge_cnt still holds k-1.
  always @(posedge clk) begin
    edge_cnt <= edge_cnt + 1;
    if ((irq8 === 1'b1) && (irq_last == 1'b0)) begin
      irq_rises     <= irq_rises + 1;
      irq_rise_edge <= edge_cnt;
    end
    irq_last <= (irq8 === 1'b1);
  end

  // Lockstep comparison of the ADDR_WIDTH 4 instance against ADDR_WIDTH 8.
  always @(negedge clk) begin
    if (lock_en) begin
      if ({awready4, wready4, bvalid4, bresp4, arready4, rvalid4, rdata4, rresp4, irq4} ===
          {awready8, wready8, bvalid8, bresp8, arready8, rvalid8, rdata8, rresp8, irq8}) begin
        lock_pass = lock_pass + 1;
      end else begin
        lock_fail = lock_fail + 1;
        $error("lockstep mismatch between ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8 at %0t", $time);
      end
    end
  end

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Check helpers
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  task chk(input ok, input [31:0] id);
    begin
      if (ok === 1'b1) begin
        passed = passed + 1;
      end else begin
        failed = failed + 1;
        $error("check %0d failed at %0t", id, $time);
      end
    end
  endtask

  task chk32(input [31:0] got, input [31:0] expv, input [31:0] id);
    begin
      if (got === expv) begin
        passed = passed + 1;
      end else begin
        failed = failed + 1;
        $error("check %0d failed at %0t: got 0x%08h, expected 0x%08h", id, $time, got, expv);
      end
    end
  endtask

  task idle(input integer n);
    integer i;
    begin
      for (i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) @(negedge clk);
    end
  endtask

  task wait_until_edge(input integer t, input [31:0] id);
    begin
      while (edge_cnt < t) @(negedge clk);
      chk32(edge_cnt, t, id);
    end
  endtask

  task wait_rise(input integer prev_n, input integer maxc, input [31:0] id);
    integer c;
    begin
      c = 0;
      while ((irq_rises == prev_n) && (c < maxc)) begin
        @(negedge clk);
        c = c + 1;
      end
      chk32(irq_rises, prev_n + 1, id);
    end
  endtask

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Bus tasks: called just after a negedge, return just after a negedge
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  task axi_write(input [7:0] addr, input [31:0] data, input [3:0] strb,
                 input integer aw_dly, input integer w_dly, input integer b_dly,
                 input [1:0] exp_resp, input [31:0] id);
    integer cyc;
    integer k;
    reg aw_ok;
    reg w_ok;
    reg hs_aw;
    reg hs_w;
    reg [1:0] resp0;
    begin
      cyc   = 0;
      aw_ok = 1'b0;
      w_ok  = 1'b0;
      while (!(aw_ok && w_ok)) begin
        if (!aw_ok && (cyc >= aw_dly)) begin
          awaddr  = addr;
          awvalid = 1'b1;
        end
        if (!w_ok && (cyc >= w_dly)) begin
          wdata  = data;
          wstrb  = strb;
          wvalid = 1'b1;
        end
        chk(bvalid8 == 1'b0, id);
        chk(awready8 == !aw_ok, id);
        chk(wready8 == !w_ok, id);
        hs_aw = awvalid && awready8;
        hs_w  = wvalid && wready8;
        @(negedge clk);
        cyc = cyc + 1;
        if (hs_aw) begin
          awvalid = 1'b0;
          aw_ok   = 1'b1;
        end
        if (hs_w) begin
          wvalid = 1'b0;
          w_ok   = 1'b1;
        end
        if (cyc > 200) begin
          chk(1'b0, id);
          awvalid = 1'b0;
          wvalid  = 1'b0;
          aw_ok   = 1'b1;
          w_ok    = 1'b1;
        end
      end
      wr_eff = edge_cnt;
      chk(bvalid8 == 1'b1, id);
      chk(bresp8 == exp_resp, id);
      resp0 = bresp8;
      for (k = 0; k < b_dly; k = k + 1) begin
        @(negedge clk);
        chk(bvalid8 == 1'b1 && bresp8 == resp0 && awready8 == 1'b0 && wready8 == 1'b0, id);
      end
      bready = 1'b1;
      @(negedge clk);
      bready = 1'b0;
      chk(bvalid8 == 1'b0, id);
      chk(awready8 == 1'b1 && wready8 == 1'b1, id);
    end
  endtask

  task wr(input [7:0] addr, input [31:0] data, input [3:0] strb,
          input [1:0] exp_resp, input [31:0] id);
    begin
      axi_write(addr, data, strb, 0, 0, 0, exp_resp, id);
    end
  endtask

  task axi_read(input [7:0] addr, input integer r_dly, input [31:0] id);
    integer cyc;
    integer k;
    reg hs;
    begin
      araddr  = addr;
      arvalid = 1'b1;
      hs      = 1'b0;
      cyc     = 0;
      while (!hs) begin
        chk(rvalid8 == 1'b0, id);
        hs = arready8;
        @(negedge clk);
        cyc = cyc + 1;
        if (cyc > 200) begin
          chk(1'b0, id);
          hs = 1'b1;
        end
      end
      arvalid = 1'b0;
      rd_edge = edge_cnt;
      chk(rvalid8 == 1'b1, id);
      chk(arready8 == 1'b0, id);
      rd_data = rdata8;
      rd_resp = rresp8;
      for (k = 0; k < r_dly; k = k + 1) begin
        @(negedge clk);
        chk(rvalid8 == 1'b1 && rdata8 == rd_data && rresp8 == rd_resp && arready8 == 1'b0, id);
      end
      rready = 1'b1;
      @(negedge clk);
      rready = 1'b0;
      chk(rvalid8 == 1'b0 && arready8 == 1'b1, id);
    end
  endtask

  task rd_chk(input [7:0] addr, input [31:0] expv, input [1:0] exp_resp, input [31:0] id);
    begin
      axi_read(addr, 0, id);
      chk32(rd_data, expv, id);
      chk(rd_resp == exp_resp, id);
    end
  endtask

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  // Test sequence
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------
  initial begin
    plus_ok = $value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce);
    if (plus_ok == 0) nonce = {(8*64){1'b0}};

    aresetn = 1'b0;
    repeat (4) @(negedge clk);
    aresetn = 1'b1;
    lock_en = 1'b1;

    // 1. Reset values
    chk(awready8 == 1'b1 && wready8 == 1'b1 && arready8 == 1'b1, 100);
    chk(bvalid8 == 1'b0 && rvalid8 == 1'b0 && irq8 == 1'b0, 101);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h0, OKAY, 102);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h0, OKAY, 103);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'h0, OKAY, 104);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h0, OKAY, 105);

    // 2. LOAD with partial strobes
    wr(8'h04, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, OKAY, 200);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, OKAY, 201);
    wr(8'h04, 32'h1234_5678, 4'b0101, OKAY, 202);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'hFF34_FF78, OKAY, 203);
    wr(8'h04, 32'hA5A5_A5A5, 4'b1010, OKAY, 204);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'hA534_A578, OKAY, 205);
    wr(8'h04, 32'h0000_0000, 4'b0000, OKAY, 206);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'hA534_A578, OKAY, 207);
    wr(8'h04, 32'hDEAD_BEEF, 4'b1000, OKAY, 208);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'hDE34_A578, OKAY, 209);

    // 3. Channel orders, backpressure, back-to-back, read+write together
    axi_write(8'h04, 32'h1111_1111, 4'hF, 0, 3, 4, OKAY, 300);
    axi_read(8'h04, 3, 301);
    chk32(rd_data, 32'h1111_1111, 302);
    chk(rd_resp == OKAY, 303);
    axi_write(8'h04, 32'h2222_2222, 4'hF, 3, 0, 2, OKAY, 304);
    axi_read(8'h04, 5, 305);
    chk32(rd_data, 32'h2222_2222, 306);
    axi_write(8'h04, 32'h3333_3333, 4'hF, 1, 0, 0, OKAY, 307);
    axi_write(8'h04, 32'h4444_4444, 4'hF, 0, 1, 0, OKAY, 308);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h4444_4444, OKAY, 309);

    awaddr  = 8'h04;
    awvalid = 1'b1;
    wdata   = 32'h5555_5555;
    wstrb   = 4'hF;
    wvalid  = 1'b1;
    araddr  = 8'h04;
    arvalid = 1'b1;
    chk(awready8 == 1'b1 && wready8 == 1'b1 && arready8 == 1'b1, 310);
    @(negedge clk);
    awvalid = 1'b0;
    wvalid  = 1'b0;
    arvalid = 1'b0;
    chk(bvalid8 == 1'b1 && bresp8 == OKAY, 311);
    chk(rvalid8 == 1'b1 && rresp8 == OKAY, 312);
    chk32(rdata8, 32'h4444_4444, 313);
    bready = 1'b1;
    rready = 1'b1;
    @(negedge clk);
    bready = 1'b0;
    rready = 1'b0;
    chk(bvalid8 == 1'b0 && rvalid8 == 1'b0, 314);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h5555_5555, OKAY, 315);

    // 4. COUNT read only, SLVERR policy, CTRL write without wstrb[0]
    wr(8'h08, 32'h1234_5678, 4'hF, SLVERR, 400);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'h0, OKAY, 401);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h5555_5555, OKAY, 402);
    wr(8'h05, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, SLVERR, 403);
    wr(8'h01, 32'h0000_0007, 4'hF, SLVERR, 404);
    wr(8'h0E, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, SLVERR, 405);
    wr(8'h03, 32'h0000_0007, 4'hF, SLVERR, 406);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h5555_5555, OKAY, 407);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h0, OKAY, 408);
    rd_chk(8'h05, 32'h0, SLVERR, 409);
    rd_chk(8'h01, 32'h0, SLVERR, 410);
    rd_chk(8'h06, 32'h0, SLVERR, 411);
    rd_chk(8'h0F, 32'h0, SLVERR, 412);
    wr(8'h00, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'b1110, OKAY, 413);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h0, OKAY, 414);
    idle(5);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'h0, OKAY, 415);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 416);

    // 5. One-shot timed to the cycle
    wr(8'h04, 32'd5, 4'hF, OKAY, 500);
    prev = irq_rises;
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 501);
    e0 = wr_eff;
    axi_read(8'h08, 0, 502);
    chk32(rd_data, 5 - (rd_edge - 1 - e0), 503);
    wait_rise(prev, 50, 504);
    chk32(irq_rise_edge, e0 + 5, 505);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b1, 506);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h2, OKAY, 507);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'h0, OKAY, 508);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h1, OKAY, 509);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h0, 4'hF, OKAY, 510);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h1, OKAY, 511);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'b1110, OKAY, 512);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h1, OKAY, 513);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b1, 514);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'b0001, OKAY, 515);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 516);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h0, OKAY, 517);
    idle(30);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 518);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev + 1, 519);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'h0, OKAY, 520);

    // 6. LOAD of 1 and of 0: one-cycle counts
    wr(8'h04, 32'd1, 4'hF, OKAY, 600);
    prev = irq_rises;
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 601);
    e0 = wr_eff;
    idle(2);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev + 1, 602);
    chk32(irq_rise_edge, e0 + 1, 603);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h2, OKAY, 604);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 605);
    wr(8'h04, 32'd0, 4'hF, OKAY, 606);
    prev = irq_rises;
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 607);
    e0 = wr_eff;
    idle(2);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev + 1, 608);
    chk32(irq_rise_edge, e0 + 1, 609);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h2, OKAY, 610);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'h0, OKAY, 611);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 612);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 613);

    // 7. Interrupt enable on a pending expiry
    wr(8'h04, 32'd3, 4'hF, OKAY, 700);
    prev = irq_rises;
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h1, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 701);
    idle(10);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 702);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev, 703);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h1, OKAY, 704);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h0, OKAY, 705);
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h2, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 706);
    e0 = wr_eff;
    chk(irq8 == 1'b1, 707);
    idle(1);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev + 1, 708);
    chk32(irq_rise_edge, e0, 709);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h2, OKAY, 710);
    wr(8'h00, 32'h0, 4'hF, OKAY, 711);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 712);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h1, OKAY, 713);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 714);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h0, OKAY, 715);

    // 8. Periodic counts over several periods
    wr(8'h04, 32'd8, 4'hF, OKAY, 800);
    prev = irq_rises;
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h7, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 801);
    e0 = wr_eff;
    for (p = 1; p <= 3; p = p + 1) begin
      wait_rise(prev, 40, 802);
      chk32(irq_rise_edge, e0 + 8 * p, 803);
      prev = irq_rises;
      e1 = irq_rise_edge;
      wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 804);
      chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 805);
      axi_read(8'h08, 0, 806);
      chk32(rd_data, 8 - (rd_edge - 1 - e1), 807);
    end
    wait_rise(prev, 40, 808);
    chk32(irq_rise_edge, e0 + 32, 809);
    // A clear landing on the edge a count ends: the expiry is kept
    wait_until_edge(e0 + 39, 810);
    axi_write(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 811);
    chk32(wr_eff, e0 + 40, 812);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b1, 813);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h1, OKAY, 814);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h7, OKAY, 815);
    prev = irq_rises;
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 816);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 817);
    wait_rise(prev, 40, 818);
    chk32(irq_rise_edge, e0 + 48, 819);
    wr(8'h00, 32'h6, 4'hF, OKAY, 820);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h6, OKAY, 821);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 822);
    prev = irq_rises;
    idle(20);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev, 823);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 824);

    // 9. Stop freezes COUNT, then restart, then restart while running
    wr(8'h04, 32'd40, 4'hF, OKAY, 900);
    prev = irq_rises;
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 901);
    e0 = wr_eff;
    idle(5);
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h2, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 902);
    s0 = wr_eff;
    exp_cnt = 40 - (s0 - e0);
    rd_chk(8'h08, exp_cnt, OKAY, 903);
    idle(60);
    rd_chk(8'h08, exp_cnt, OKAY, 904);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h2, OKAY, 905);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev, 906);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 907);
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 908);
    e1 = wr_eff;
    idle(10);
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 909);
    e2 = wr_eff;
    chk(e2 > e1, 910);
    wait_rise(prev, 80, 911);
    chk32(irq_rise_edge, e2 + 40, 912);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h2, OKAY, 913);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 914);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 915);

    // 10a. One-shot: restart written on the edge the count ends
    wr(8'h04, 32'd10, 4'hF, OKAY, 1000);
    prev = irq_rises;
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 1001);
    e0 = wr_eff;
    wait_until_edge(e0 + 9, 1002);
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 1003);
    chk32(wr_eff, e0 + 10, 1004);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b1, 1005);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev + 1, 1006);
    chk32(irq_rise_edge, e0 + 10, 1007);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h3, OKAY, 1008);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 1009);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 1010);
    prev = irq_rises;
    wait_rise(prev, 40, 1011);
    chk32(irq_rise_edge, e0 + 20, 1012);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h2, OKAY, 1013);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 1014);

    // 10b. Periodic: stop written on the edge the count ends
    wr(8'h04, 32'd6, 4'hF, OKAY, 1020);
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h7, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 1021);
    e0 = wr_eff;
    wait_until_edge(e0 + 5, 1022);
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h6, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 1023);
    chk32(wr_eff, e0 + 6, 1024);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b1, 1025);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h6, OKAY, 1026);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'd6, OKAY, 1027);
    idle(20);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'd6, OKAY, 1028);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 1029);
    prev = irq_rises;
    idle(20);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev, 1030);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 1031);

    // 10c. One-shot: stop written on the edge the count ends
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 1040);
    e0 = wr_eff;
    wait_until_edge(e0 + 5, 1041);
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h2, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 1042);
    chk32(wr_eff, e0 + 6, 1043);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b1, 1044);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h2, OKAY, 1045);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'd0, OKAY, 1046);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'd1, OKAY, 1047);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1, 4'hF, OKAY, 1048);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 1049);

    // 11. Reset during a count, with a held write address
    wr(8'h04, 32'd50, 4'hF, OKAY, 1100);
    axi_write(8'h00, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0, OKAY, 1101);
    idle(10);
    awaddr  = 8'h04;
    awvalid = 1'b1;
    @(negedge clk);
    awvalid = 1'b0;
    chk(awready8 == 1'b0 && wready8 == 1'b1 && bvalid8 == 1'b0, 1102);
    aresetn = 1'b0;
    repeat (3) @(negedge clk);
    aresetn = 1'b1;
    chk(awready8 == 1'b1 && wready8 == 1'b1 && arready8 == 1'b1, 1103);
    chk(bvalid8 == 1'b0 && rvalid8 == 1'b0 && irq8 == 1'b0, 1104);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h0, OKAY, 1105);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h0, OKAY, 1106);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'h0, OKAY, 1107);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h0, OKAY, 1108);
    wdata  = 32'h0000_0099;
    wstrb  = 4'hF;
    wvalid = 1'b1;
    @(negedge clk);
    wvalid = 1'b0;
    chk(wready8 == 1'b0 && awready8 == 1'b1, 1109);
    repeat (3) begin
      @(negedge clk);
      chk(bvalid8 == 1'b0, 1110);
    end
    awaddr  = 8'h04;
    awvalid = 1'b1;
    @(negedge clk);
    awvalid = 1'b0;
    chk(bvalid8 == 1'b1 && bresp8 == OKAY, 1111);
    bready = 1'b1;
    @(negedge clk);
    bready = 1'b0;
    chk(bvalid8 == 1'b0, 1112);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h0000_0099, OKAY, 1113);
    prev = irq_rises;
    idle(60);
    chk32(irq_rises, prev, 1114);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'h0, OKAY, 1115);

    // 12. Offsets from 0x10 up at ADDR_WIDTH 8 (lockstep off: they alias at 4)
    wr(8'h04, 32'h5A5A_5A5A, 4'hF, OKAY, 1200);
    lock_en = 1'b0;
    wr(8'h10, 32'h0000_0007, 4'hF, SLVERR, 1201);
    wr(8'h14, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, SLVERR, 1202);
    wr(8'h18, 32'h1234_5678, 4'hF, SLVERR, 1203);
    wr(8'h1C, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, SLVERR, 1204);
    wr(8'h80, 32'h0000_0003, 4'hF, SLVERR, 1205);
    wr(8'hF4, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, SLVERR, 1206);
    wr(8'hFC, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, SLVERR, 1207);
    rd_chk(8'h10, 32'h0, SLVERR, 1208);
    rd_chk(8'h14, 32'h0, SLVERR, 1209);
    rd_chk(8'h18, 32'h0, SLVERR, 1210);
    rd_chk(8'h1C, 32'h0, SLVERR, 1211);
    rd_chk(8'h40, 32'h0, SLVERR, 1212);
    rd_chk(8'h84, 32'h0, SLVERR, 1213);
    rd_chk(8'hF0, 32'h0, SLVERR, 1214);
    rd_chk(8'hFC, 32'h0, SLVERR, 1215);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h0, OKAY, 1216);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h5A5A_5A5A, OKAY, 1217);
    rd_chk(8'h0C, 32'h0, OKAY, 1218);
    idle(10);
    rd_chk(8'h08, 32'h0, OKAY, 1219);
    chk(irq8 == 1'b0, 1220);
    aresetn = 1'b0;
    repeat (3) @(negedge clk);
    aresetn = 1'b1;
    lock_en = 1'b1;
    chk(irq4 == 1'b0 && bvalid4 == 1'b0 && rvalid4 == 1'b0, 1221);
    rd_chk(8'h00, 32'h0, OKAY, 1222);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h0, OKAY, 1223);
    wr(8'h04, 32'h0BAD_F00D, 4'hF, OKAY, 1224);
    rd_chk(8'h04, 32'h0BAD_F00D, OKAY, 1225);

    idle(2);
    $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce,
             passed + lock_pass, failed + lock_fail);
    $finish;
  end

  // Watchdog
  initial begin
    #2000000;
    $error("watchdog timeout at %0t", $time);
    $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce,
             passed + lock_pass, failed + lock_fail + 1);
    $finish;
  end

endmodule
